      "writtenOn": "2020-07-30T04:12:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Current behavior is that if no U2F keys are present, device will be considered in FIPS-approved mode by default. However, this is incorrect until U2F key gen is merged ( https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/2262055), which is going to change due to need to change storage location of U2F keys to be AP RO. However, there is https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/2327960  which use some functions from FIPS which won\u0027t work if FIPS power-up tests aren\u0027t completed as https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/2262055 is not included to prod without 2262055. This patch disables logic to switch to FIPS-approved mode if no U2F keys on platform (always return FIPS-not-approved mode), but run power-up tests. This is a workaround to have prod build with newer webauthn code and at the same time test FIPS initialization code. Side-effect of cherry-picking CLs in prod.",
      "parentUuid": "1bf3223a_df6786f3",
      "revId": "09544f8e9dd92935a027b46b3773ace6b31ad039",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
